{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-project-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48: `rates-project`, the Rates-scale twin of `scale-project` -- running and start Total Energy for the gasoline-selected passenger car on the PROJECT database's one link (road type 4, 30 mph) in Washtenaw County, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>` and `<modeldomain value=\"PROJECT\"/>`. Captured with the execution database named `MOVESExecution` (`run-moves.sh`'s EXECUTION_DB_NAME), because RatePostProcessorRatesFirst.sql's PROJECT branch hardcodes that name and the corpus' per-host name stops it with every rate table empty.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. PROJECT domain has no speed bins: MOVES synthesizes no links, BaseRateGenerator turns `useAvgSpeedBin` off, and the post-processor divides emissionRate by the LINK's average speed. So RatePerDistance is the inventory's per-hour rate over the cohort's share (`rtRate_direct`) over 30 mph, one row per cohort on link 1 at avgSpeedBinID 0 -- measured, `scale-project`'s inventory over the cohort's SHO per real day over 30 is the rate, 125 of 125 within 2e-06. RatePerStart and StartsPerVehicle are skipped in PROJECT domain, and the run's start energy has no off-network link to happen on.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `scale-project`'s, plus `n_ratesScale` = 1.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "project-domain",
      "rates",
      "rates-project"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, monthID 8.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 9. `<beginhour key=\"8\">` is a 0-based index into the sorted hour list (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_aggregationhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_aggregationhour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The hours the run aggregates over. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspechour` itself and the same file.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspechourday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, dayID 5 (weekday). The second factor of the activity axis and of the output axis, and its extent is one in this run: `<day id=\"5\">` selects one day type where the earlier `<day key=\"5\">` was an out-of-range INDEX and fell back to both (moves.rs PR #55).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_rateday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_rateday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The day types the RATE-side time pre-aggregation is scoped to. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspecday` itself and the same file: the pre-aggregation averages over one cell and returns the table's own value. A run that aggregates points this somewhere else, because MOVES overwrites `runspecday` with the synthesized output day AFTER the pre-aggregation has run.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_actday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_actday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The day types the output day's ACTIVITY covers. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspecday` itself and the same file, and `noOfRealDays` is that one day type's.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecsourcetype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-project/tables/db__movesexecution__runspecsourcetype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecsourcetype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, sourceTypeID 21.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecroadtype": {
      "kind": "static",
